":"Paris","local_city":"Paris"}],"contract_type":"internship","social_image":"https://imagen.welcometothejungle.com/api/generate-image?data=%7B%22contractType%22%3A%22internship%22%2C%22coverImage%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fcdn-images.welcometothejungle.com%2F2rEE5izgH4IDvrXMCY0IvU18fjzf_edzvDur98n3bSs%2Frs%3Aauto%3A1200%3A627%3A%2Fq%3A85%2FczM6Ly93dHRqLXByb2R1Y3Rpb24vdXBsb2Fkcy93ZWJzaXRlX29yZ2FuaXphdGlvbi9jb3Zlcl9pbWFnZS93dHRqX2ZyL2VuLWNiMTRjNTAwLWUxYWQtNDk2ZS1hOGZmLTk3OGQ1ZDRjZDAyNi5qcGc%22%2C%22logo%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fcdn-images.welcometothejungle.com%2FwjGstoYHeV2BgIsVRGeSA2VLijuJQetvOpfkRsNQcOg%2Frs%3Aauto%3A400%3A%3A%2Fq%3A85%2FczM6Ly93dHRqLXByb2R1Y3Rpb24vdXBsb2Fkcy9vcmdhbml6YXRpb24vbG9nby82ODMyLzE1MjE1NS84MDJlNDA3NS1hMzdiLTQ5MjktYmUzZi0xZWYxN2FhY2ZhNjcucG5n%22%2C%22name%22%3A%22Internship%20-%20Data%20Analyst%20%2F%20Analytics%20Engineer%22%2C%22office%22%3A%22Paris%22%2C%22organizationName%22%3A%22OVRSEA%22%2C%22remote%22%3A%22partial%22%7D&locale=en-US&template-id=wttj-job-og-image&token=bdd665140c594aea42ce767c159ddcdd45e583faabd6f93af9b91b745b2c887b","remote":"partial","salary_max":null,"company_description":null,"benefits":{},"experience_level":null,"description":"<p></p><h3><strong>Our mission: to make international freight simpler and more sustainable through technology!</strong></h3><p>Founded in 2017, OVRSEA is a next-generation freight forwarder that uses technology to simplify and optimize international transport for businesses. We support 700+ companies across 60 countries in their international freight shipments.</p><p>In January 2026, OVRSEA merged with the Fatton Lyseo group. This large-scale operation comes amid profound geopolitical, commercial, and technological shifts. Our ambition is clear: to build, through organic and external growth, a unified, agile, and sustainable French leader in logistics, capable of addressing new challenges in logistics control, operational performance, and technological disruption.</p><p>This merger brings together, under a single group, cutting-edge tech expertise, well-established historical know-how, and a dense network of locations across strategic geographies - with over 1,000 employees, 61 offices in 14 countries, and 120,000 m² of warehouse space - serving demanding clients in the luxury, pharmaceutical, cosmetics, and food industries. Joining our teams means taking part in building an independent, high-performing, and innovative group.</p><p></p><h3><strong>💻 The Data Team at OVRSEA</strong></h3><p></p><p>OVRSEA operates with a lean, centralized data team that serves as the single source of truth for all company data, from operational metrics to sales and financial information.</p><p>We are at a pivotal moment: with the merger, the group is scaling from ~100 to over 1,000 people, across several entities and systems. The Data team&#39;s challenge is to scale data usage accordingly (more users, more entities, more tools) while keeping a single, reliable source of truth for every key business metric.</p><p>The Data team&#39;s main objectives are to serve every team in the company and help them make data-driven decisions. This includes:</p><ul><li><strong>Fostering Data culture</strong>: encouraging data consumption and literacy across the organization</li><li><strong>Ensuring quality Data access</strong>: making reliable data easily accessible to everyone in the group</li><li><strong>Breaking Data silos</strong>: implementing centralized Data Governance to establish single sources of truth for key business metrics across entities</li><li><strong>Building Data infrastructure</strong>: maintaining robust data pipelines and systems that enable scalable analytics</li><li><strong>Bridging Product and Data</strong>: making sure the data we expose keeps pace with a fast-evolving product. The product changes quickly, and the Data team must stay agile and adapt continuously.</li></ul><p></p><p> </p><h3><strong>🎒 Your missions inside the Data Team</strong></h3><p></p><p>You&#39;ll work hand in hand with Marie-Sophie, Head of Data at OVRSEA. Your missions:</p><p><em>Creating and Maintaining Data models:</em></p><ul><li>Building transformed, analytics-ready datasets using dbt and SQL</li><li>Ensuring models are well-documented, tested, and follow dbt best practices</li><li>Implementing data quality checks and monitoring</li></ul><p><em>Deploying and Scaling our BI Platform (Sigma):</em></p><ul><li>Building and organizing official, group-level dashboards in Sigma</li><li>Ensuring there is only one source of truth in Sigma for users: official, owned dashboards, with no duplicated metrics or competing versions of the numbers</li><li>Monitoring performance and usage patterns</li></ul><p><em>Building the Single Source of Truth for Company Context:</em></p><ul><li>Beyond the numbers themselves, creating the single source of truth for the company&#39;s business context: one metric = one definition, documented, owned, and shared across all entities</li><li>Structuring business knowledge (definitions, documentation, ownership) so that both humans and AI agents can rely on it</li><li>Ensuring consistency between what the data says and how teams across the group understand and use it</li></ul><p><em>Scaling the Data Team&#39;s impact through automation and AI:</em></p><ul><li>Working daily with AI coding tools (e.g. Claude Code)</li><li>Identifying repetitive or manual tasks within the data lifecycle and designing scalable automation solutions</li><li>Building and experimenting with AI agents that streamline data workflows: model documentation, data quality monitoring, first-line support to business users</li><li>Contributing to AI-powered self-service experiences on top of our BI platform (e.g. text-to-insight), so business teams can explore data autonomously</li></ul><p></p><p></p><h3> </h3><h3>🤝 We&#39;re meant to work together if</h3><p></p><p></p><ul><li>You are available for <strong>6 months</strong>, starting as early as December 2026.</li><li>You are a student from a top business or engineering school (or equivalent). We value the intersection of technical and business expertise.</li><li>Excellent <strong>communication</strong> skills: you know how to bridge the gap between technical teams and business users, and can make data topics clear to both audiences.</li><li><strong>Rigorous</strong>: you care deeply about data quality. You go after edge cases, dig until the numbers are right, and deliver precise, reliable work.</li><li>Familiarity with BI tools (Sigma, Metabase, Tableau, or similar)</li><li>Basic development tools (Git, terminal, command line)</li><li><strong>SQL</strong> proficiency and/or experience with dbt</li><li>Enthusiasm for <strong>AI tools</strong>: you&#39;re curious about working with AI assistants and agents day-to-day</li><li>Curiosity and strong desire to learn. You don&#39;t need to master all technical skills initially, but must have a strong willingness to learn.</li><li>Fluent in French and English (both written and spoken)</li></ul><p></p><p></p><h3><strong>Why join us at OVRSEA? 💚</strong></h3><p></p><ul><li>Be part of our team of ambitious and talented individuals who share our values: analytical thinking, quality execution, and a deep thirst for learning.</li><li>Experience a personalized onboarding program, setting you up for success from day one.</li><li>Work in a vibrant work environment and take on challenging projects, collaborating with other teams while enjoying a high level of ownership and autonomy.</li><li>Benefit from commuter benefits and meal vouchers. For interns in France: Digital Swile card of 10€ per worked day (5,5€ paid by OVRSEA).</li><li>Engage in exciting events, including weekly culture presentations (the famous OVRSEA “PICs”), learning sessions, team rituals, and great parties!</li></ul><p> </p><p></p><h3><strong>Still not convinced? 👀</strong></h3><p>Discover our story, our product, our teams, and our commitments by visiting <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/2a725e3ef7ea4fffb97cad2352e54faa?pvs=21\"><strong>this Notion page</strong>.</a></p><p>It will give you insight into our culture and our core value, Pedagogy, also known as Learning Together, through <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ovrsea_%C3%A7a-fait-quoi-de-bosser-chez-ovrsea-activity-6811209179756302336-FdU1/\"><strong>a short video</strong></a>. You will see how we bring this value to life every day through webinars, team rituals, cultural presentations, a structured onboarding process, and our training program, the Transport Academy, designed to help you discover, or rediscover, the exciting world of international transportation.</p><p>You would like to join us? Hesitate no longer and apply to join the crazy Ovrsea adventure!</p><h3><strong>Our recruitment process 💬</strong></h3><p></p><p></p><ul><li>First call with Marie-Sophie, Head of Data, to introduce OVRSEA, discuss the internship, and learn about your expectations and motivations (30&#39;)</li><li>Live technical case study with our team (1h to 1h30)</li><li>Final round/ Speed Recruiting: meet a colleague from another team and OVRSEA&#39;s CTO (1h)</li><li>The final proposal ! 🙌</li></ul><em>At Ovrsea, we are committed to an inclusive recruitment process and to fostering diversity within our teams.</em><p></p><p> </p><p> </p><p><em>At Ovrsea, we are committed to an inclusive recruitment process and to fostering diversity within our teams.</em></p>","archived_at":"2026-05-12T03:00:06Z","salary_min":null,"featured_page":{"type":"plus","slug":"/lesplus-1"},"team":null,"recruiter_proposal":null,"summary":"","education_level":null,"office":{"address":"22 Rue Louis Blanc, 75010 Paris, France","local_address":"22 Rue Louis Blanc, 75010 Paris, France","city":"Paris","latitude":48.88052,"longitude":2.36637,"country_code":"FR","zip_code":"75010","district":"Paris","local_district":"Paris","local_city":"Paris"